3. Five-year history is the default and configurable.
4. History retrieval, coverage, warm-up, and indicators work correctly.
5. News research is sourced, timestamped, deduplicated, commodity-aware, and freshness-aware.
6. Historical scenarios are point-in-time safe and statistically transparent.
7. Gemini is default for new installs and settings are configurable.
8. Agent outputs are validated in an auditable workflow.
9. Deterministic risk/publication gates are enforced.
10. Critical tests pass or failures/blockers are explicitly documented.
11. Setup, credentials, limitations, architecture, and troubleshooting are documented.
12. No fabricated sources, market data, statistics, or test results are introduced.

## 14. Implementation roadmap

**Phase A — Discovery:** inspect repository, baseline, providers/limits, design/test note.  
**Phase B — Commodity foundation:** canonical registry, silver/oil mappings, refactor gold-only assumptions, tests.  
**Phase C — History/charts:** five-year default/selector, pagination, coverage, warm-up, indicator/resampling fixes, performance tests.  
**Phase D — Evidence/news:** approved-source ingestion, provenance, deduplication, taxonomy, causal sentiment, freshness, source-failure handling.  
**Phase E — Historical scenarios:** point-in-time-safe event studies, regimes, analogues, distributions, excursion statistics, caveats.  
**Phase F — LLM/agents:** Gemini default, provider abstraction, secure settings/test UI, bounded agents, schemas, budgets, audit, critic, publication gate.  
**Phase G — Advisory integration:** combine technical/news/sentiment/fundamental/history/risk for swing and long-term; preserve gold and stale-price regression tests.  
**Phase H — UX/release:** dashboard, chart settings, evidence views, advisory details, responsive/accessibility states, documentation, migrations, full validation.

A phase is not complete merely because files were created. Implement and test each deliverable as far as provider access and environment permit.

